Gametek are aware of these bugs and will provide a patch disk to anyone who calss them +(44) 1753 553445.
This disk fixes most of the major bugs and makes the game playable and enjoyable.

The bug with joystick calibration is known but not addressed. Your problem may be running your joystick
from your sound card joystick port. If you run the game with no sound then you should find that the 
joystick works. If you want sound and your joystick then you can start the game, load a saved position
with you in-flight and well away from anything you can hit and adjust the trim controls on your joystick until the
ship stops spinning (this works for me) alternately you could try installing a seperate game port on your machine
( have'nt tried this yet).

Patch disks (and much other useful information about frontier)  can be obtained at the following URL
	http://www.maths.tcd.ie/~ratava/frontier/ffe.html

